                                "sense_id": "778ea735-a846-3dff-bdc7-8d4234e009b9",
                                "text": "Turner and West ( 1968 ) suggest that the phases of an interglacial period (cryocratic, protocratic, mesocratic, telocratic ) be considered as cenozones."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1a0ac0f2-b843-42a6-805f-5f6d31730297",
                                "sense_id": "778ea735-a846-3dff-bdc7-8d4234e009b9",
                                "text": "Hence, regional soil degenerations and podsolization was probably an important factor contributing to the retrogressive change in the forest composition at the end of the mesocratic phase.."
                            },
